        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/ba8739/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-31T17:36:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>One of the most common powers in super-hero stories is the power to fly, which has almost no bearing on SofM. I was wondering if there was any word on how could, and who couldn’t fly in the multiverse. Here are my thoughts, presented mostly as a starting point:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Heroes:</p><p>Absolute Zero: - Thermodynamics battlesuit.&nbsp; Either flies on a jet of fire, or does the ice-slide thing</p><p>Fanatic:</p><p>Legacy:</p><p>Ra: A god.&nbsp; Either flies directly, or has a chariot or sky boat.</p><p>Tempest: Super Hero Types who generally fly – Aliens, and Weather Controllers.</p><p>Visionary: Telekinetic flight</p><p>Argent Adept: Big billowy cloak demands flying, and gentle touchdowns to Dubstep.</p><p>Omnitron X: Cosmic Omnitron flew.&nbsp; Seems like Exie would keep that upgrade</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Villains:</p><p>Flipped Baron Blade: Battlesuits generally fly.</p><p>Citizen Dawn:</p><p>Grand Warlord Voss: Battlesuit or alien.&nbsp; Either way</p><p>Matriarch: Dominant, predatory, flightless birds are so 62 million years ago.&nbsp; Cloak propels her at 20 knots, the speed of an unladen European Swallow.</p><p>Apostate:</p><p>Gloomweaver: Demon of nightmares.&nbsp; He flies because we don’t don’t don’t want him to</p><p>La Capitan: Little Anti-grav harnesses borrowed here or there.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:37:51.146Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
